<http://data.silknow.org/event/3081dcb9-9747-396e-932a-c500bb853336>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Registered File number 1990/45.\nThe pattern is loosely based on European dress silks of the 1760s and this silk could date from the 1830s-40s or the 1890s, both periods in the 19th century when 18th century patterns were especially fashionable. \n\nThis unused piece of high quality would have been made to hang on walls rather than for other domestic purposes."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/1ce17939-36c7-3558-88c4-c2d211c21883> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Given by Mrs V. Morton" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/96956d78-924e-327e-9b49-459dbff4ae90> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Registered File number 1990/45.\nThe pattern is loosely based on European dress silks of the 1760s and this silk could date from the 1830s-40s or the 1890s, both periods in the 19th century when 18th century patterns were especially fashionable. \n\nThis unused piece of high quality would have been made to hang on walls rather than for other domestic purposes."@en .

